      "title": "READ ME",
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.8",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# [READ ME] RefMod Audio Pack (MiniMax H3)\n\n## What this does\nSaves a sound as a **RefMod** you can load in the **MM RefMod T2V** workflow, so the same music, ambience or sound effect shows up across many videos.\n\n**Voice cloning does not work reliably yet.** The node author's own tests could not copy a speaker's voice. Music and ambience do work. For a fixed character voice, keep using your TTS voice clone.\n\n## Picking the audio\n1. Use a **clean** clip: one sound only, no talking over the music, no clicks or silence at the start.\n2. Only the **first 30 seconds** are used (`max_seconds`). Trim the file so the part you want comes first.\n3. 5 to 15 seconds of clean audio is a good starting point. Longer is not automatically better.\n\n## How to use\n1. **AUDIO FILE:** click upload and choose your file.\n2. **CREATE REFMOD:** type a name in `name` (for example `lofi_beat`). `concept_type` is only a label, pick whatever fits.\n3. **SAVE REFMOD:** `subfolder` = `audio` saves it to `models/refmods/audio/<name>`.\n4. **Queue.**\n5. In the T2V workflow: click **Refresh RefMods**, then **+ Add RefMod** on the CHARACTER REFMOD node and pick it. Describe the sound in your prompt too (for example `non_diegetic_music: lo-fi beat playing in the background`).\n\n## Good to know\nAudio costs about 80 tokens per second. If you raise `max_seconds` past about 60, also raise `max_tokens` (5120), or it stops with a budget error.\n\n## Links\n- **YouTube:** [youtube.com/@lora-tech](https://www.youtube.com/@lora-tech)\n- **Discord (community, support, 1 on 1 coaching):** [discord.gg/2bqQXKxsxg](https://discord.gg/2bqQXKxsxg)\n- **Patreon:** [patreon.com/LoRAtech](https://www.patreon.com/LoRAtech)\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "# [READ ME] RefMod Audio Pack (MiniMax H3)\n\n## What this does\nSaves a sound as a **RefMod** you can load in the **MM RefMod T2V** workflow, so the same music, ambience or sound effect shows up across many videos.\n\n**Voice cloning does not work reliably yet.** The node author's own tests could not copy a speaker's voice. Music and ambience do work. For a fixed character voice, keep using your TTS voice clone.\n\n## Picking the audio\n1. Use a **clean** clip: one sound only, no talking over the music, no clicks or silence at the start.\n2. Only the **first 30 seconds** are used (`max_seconds`). Trim the file so the part you want comes first.\n3. 5 to 15 seconds of clean audio is a good starting point. Longer is not automatically better.\n\n## How to use\n1. **AUDIO FILE:** click upload and choose your file.\n2. **CREATE REFMOD:** type a name in `name` (for example `lofi_beat`). `concept_type` is only a label, pick whatever fits.\n3. **SAVE REFMOD:** `subfolder` = `audio` saves it to `models/refmods/audio/<name>`.\n4. **Queue.**\n5. In the T2V workflow: click **Refresh RefMods**, then **+ Add RefMod** on the CHARACTER REFMOD node and pick it. Describe the sound in your prompt too (for example `non_diegetic_music: lo-fi beat playing in the background`).\n\n## Good to know\nAudio costs about 80 tokens per second. If you raise `max_seconds` past about 60, also raise `max_tokens` (5120), or it stops with a budget error.\n\n## Links\n- **YouTube:** [youtube.com/@lora-tech](https://www.youtube.com/@lora-tech)\n- **Discord (community, support, 1 on 1 coaching):** [discord.gg/2bqQXKxsxg](https://discord.gg/2bqQXKxsxg)\n- **Patreon:** [patreon.com/LoRAtech](https://www.patreon.com/LoRAtech)\n"
      },
